where everyone affected run away from the location, remembering a scary animal instead of whatever actually happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T06:28:38-08:00","id":1183566,"title":"","content":"IIRC most Animalism powers are knowledge and direction. There is no Animalism power that calms/enrages an animal at the drop of a hat, so you could do that. There is a devotion I think for sleeping inside an animal (melding), though I could be remembering WoD there. Actually take a look at the wiki for Animalism in Masquerade/Dark Ages for inspiration; you mind find some other good ideas there.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T09:39:36-08:00","id":1183619,"title":"","content":"Actually there is a nice devotion in ATYoN: basically you feed a certain amount of vitae from a specific animal (summoned with Animalism 3), then you can have sensory flash from any animal of that kind in a really hige range. Concentrating and spending vitae you also have other effect like commanding them at distance (not really sure I need to check).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T09:52:37-08:00","id":1183622,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of things to do with Animalism devotions. <br /> <br /> Transfer a vinculum bound thrall's consciousness into an animal. <br /> <br /> Enable animal minions to use Protean 1. (The animal minions hide in the ground and the Gangel master lures a target to the area where they erupt from the ground.)<br /> <br /> Enable animal minions to count as the caster for Cruac or Theban Sorcery spellcasting. (One time per use of the devotion.) <br /> <br /> Enable animal minions to count as the user for discipline ranges or eye contact requirements for a time frame. Etc.<br /> <br /> Enable a designated animal minion to become the automatic target for others' discipline use equal to the number of successes on activation.<br /> <br /> Designate 4 animal minions to act as an extension of the borders of Lord of the Land. Or Feral Infection vector where effects emanate from the minion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T13:11:41-08:00","id":1183678,"title":"","content":"Looking at the Discipline, Animalism has powers that relate to animals (obviously) and also marking or claim territory.<ul><li>(+Nightmare) Leverage Nightmare's illusionary powers to make animals seem more fearsome or to &quot;haunt&quot; a target, driving them insane (think Edgar Allen Poe's The Raven).</li> <li>(+Vigor?) Charge an animal with pressurized blood/Vitae, sending them to a target like a guided (gory) bomb. A more advanced version might even send a &quot;volley&quot; of animal-blood-rockets at foes.</li> <li>(+Auspex) Mark an area and detect any intruders.</li> <li>(+Dominate) Mark an area and impose some edict upon any who enter.</li> <li>(+Majesty) Have animals flock to you and love you. Wear them as a cloak. Or armor.</li> <li>(+Protean) Meld animals together into some monstrous Chimera. Enrollment in a Fleshcrafters' Fair optional.</li> <li>(+Obfuscate) Animal Spies.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-08-2018, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T09:09:44-08:00","id":1183959,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--